        "original_id": "993047d6-b069-5d56-b4d7-47fe9797838f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Roxie Hart, Chicago, Chicago Gal\n- People: William A. Wellman, Ginger Rogers, Adolphe Menjou, George Montgomery, Nigel Bruce, Phil Silvers, William Frawley, Spring Byington, Beulah Annan\n- Topics: Film adaptations, stage musical adaptations, Academy Award for Best Picture\n\nFacts:\n- In 1927, the play inspired by Beulah Annan was adapted into a silent film titled Chicago.\n- In 1942, Roxie Hart, also known as Chicago or Chicago Gal, was released as an American comedy film.\n- In 1942, Roxie Hart was directed by William A. Wellman.\n- In 1942, Roxie Hart starred Ginger Rogers, Adolphe Menjou, George Montgomery, Nigel Bruce, Phil Silvers, William Frawley, and Spring Byington.\n- In 1975, the play inspired by Beulah Annan was adapted into a stage musical titled Chicago.\n- In 2002, the play inspired by Beulah Annan was adapted into a movie musical titled Chicago.\n- In 2002, the movie musical Chicago won the Academy Award for Best Picture.\n- Phil Silvers was an American entertainer and comedic actor.\n- Phil Silvers was born on May 11, 1911, and died on November 1, 1985.\n- Phil Silvers was known as \"The King of Chutzpah\".",
